IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `saz-law`
IMPORT `saz-seat`

-- Tests for the SAZV / SG § 30c encoding. Expected values are written from the deposited text (SG § 30c, SAZV § 1 and Anlage, the gazette), not from this encoding's output.
-- Arguments to `the soldier who`, in order: serves within the remit of the Ministry of Defence, establishment, assigned there for international tasks,
-- activity listed in section 30c(4), overtime hours this month, hours blocked by compelling service reasons.
-- P is `as printed`; V is `without the establishment the 2025 amending regulation added`.

§ `The annex as printed`

-- The annex has 88 rows; row 27 is Headquarters Joint Support and Enabling Command; row 88 is the Zentrum für Sicherheitspolitik (sazv-anlage.txt lines 4 to 91).
#ASSERT count `the rows of the annex as printed` EQUALS 88
#ASSERT any (GIVEN row YIELD row's `number` EQUALS 27 AND row's `establishment` EQUALS "Headquarters Joint Support and Enabling Command" AND row's `state` EQUALS "Deutschland") `the rows of the annex as printed`
#ASSERT any (GIVEN row YIELD row's `number` EQUALS 88 AND row's `establishment` EQUALS "Zentrum für Sicherheitspolitik") `the rows of the annex as printed`
#ASSERT any (GIVEN row YIELD row's `number` EQUALS 76 AND row's `establishment` EQUALS "Supreme Headquarters Allied Powers Europe") `the rows of the annex as printed`
#ASSERT `the establishment is listed in the annex under the reading` `as printed` "NATO Defence College"
#ASSERT NOT (`the establishment is listed in the annex under the reading` `as printed` "Zentrum Innere Führung")
-- Without the entry the 2025 regulation added: JSEC drops out and the rest stays.
#ASSERT NOT (`the establishment is listed in the annex under the reading` `without the establishment the 2025 amending regulation added` "Headquarters Joint Support and Enabling Command")
#ASSERT `the establishment is listed in the annex under the reading` `without the establishment the 2025 amending regulation added` "Supreme Headquarters Allied Powers Europe"

§ `The article's captain at JSEC: ten hours of overtime`

-- On the annex as printed, the exemption in § 1(2) SAZV takes him out of § 30c(1) to (3) SG: no time off.
#ASSERT NOT (`section 30c(1) to (3) SG apply to the soldier under the reading` `as printed` (`the soldier who` TRUE "Headquarters Joint Support and Enabling Command" TRUE FALSE 10 0))
#ASSERT `the hours of time off to be given under the reading` `as printed` (`the soldier who` TRUE "Headquarters Joint Support and Enabling Command" TRUE FALSE 10 0) EQUALS 0
-- If the 2025 listing is void, § 30c(2) gives him time off for all ten hours (more than five hours in the month; "für diese Mehrarbeit").
#ASSERT `section 30c(1) to (3) SG apply to the soldier under the reading` `without the establishment the 2025 amending regulation added` (`the soldier who` TRUE "Headquarters Joint Support and Enabling Command" TRUE FALSE 10 0)
#ASSERT `the hours of time off to be given under the reading` `without the establishment the 2025 amending regulation added` (`the soldier who` TRUE "Headquarters Joint Support and Enabling Command" TRUE FALSE 10 0) EQUALS 10
-- If an exception is accepted the listing stands.
#ASSERT `the hours of time off to be given under the reading` (`the reading of the annex to apply` TRUE) (`the soldier who` TRUE "Headquarters Joint Support and Enabling Command" TRUE FALSE 10 0) EQUALS 0
-- Posted to JSEC but not to perform international or supranational tasks: § 1(2) does not reach him.
#ASSERT `the hours of time off to be given under the reading` `as printed` (`the soldier who` TRUE "Headquarters Joint Support and Enabling Command" FALSE FALSE 10 0) EQUALS 10

§ `An establishment that stays in the annex, and one that was never in it`

-- SHAPE is in the annex under both readings: excluded under both.
#ASSERT NOT (`section 30c(1) to (3) SG apply to the soldier under the reading` `as printed` (`the soldier who` TRUE "Supreme Headquarters Allied Powers Europe" TRUE FALSE 10 0))
#ASSERT NOT (`section 30c(1) to (3) SG apply to the soldier under the reading` `without the establishment the 2025 amending regulation added` (`the soldier who` TRUE "Supreme Headquarters Allied Powers Europe" TRUE FALSE 10 0))
-- An establishment not in the annex: § 30c(1) to (3) apply, under both readings.
#ASSERT `the hours of time off to be given under the reading` `as printed` (`the soldier who` TRUE "Zentrum Innere Führung" TRUE FALSE 10 0) EQUALS 10
#ASSERT `the hours of time off to be given under the reading` `without the establishment the 2025 amending regulation added` (`the soldier who` TRUE "Zentrum Innere Führung" TRUE FALSE 10 0) EQUALS 10

§ `§ 30c(2): the five-hour threshold and the compelling-reasons limit`

-- "mehr als fünf Stunden": five hours is not enough; more than five gives time off for all of it.
#ASSERT `the hours of time off to be given under the reading` `as printed` (`the soldier who` TRUE "Zentrum Innere Führung" FALSE FALSE 5 0) EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the hours of time off to be given under the reading` `as printed` (`the soldier who` TRUE "Zentrum Innere Führung" FALSE FALSE 5.5 0) EQUALS 5.5
#ASSERT `the hours of time off to be given under the reading` `as printed` (`the soldier who` TRUE "Zentrum Innere Führung" FALSE FALSE 6 0) EQUALS 6
-- "soweit sie aus zwingenden dienstlichen Gründen nicht möglich ist": only to the extent that compelling service reasons make it impossible.
#ASSERT `the hours of time off to be given under the reading` `as printed` (`the soldier who` TRUE "Zentrum Innere Führung" FALSE FALSE 10 4) EQUALS 6
#ASSERT `the hours of time off to be given under the reading` `as printed` (`the soldier who` TRUE "Zentrum Innere Führung" FALSE FALSE 10 10) EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the hours of time off to be given under the reading` `as printed` (`the soldier who` TRUE "Zentrum Innere Führung" FALSE FALSE 10 12) EQUALS 0
-- § 30c(4): an activity on the list takes subsections (1) to (3) away.
#ASSERT `the hours of time off to be given under the reading` `as printed` (`the soldier who` TRUE "Zentrum Innere Führung" FALSE TRUE 10 0) EQUALS 0
-- The period within which time off must be given: one year, or six months where the shorter period has been set.
#ASSERT `the months within which time off must be given` FALSE EQUALS 12
#ASSERT `the months within which time off must be given` TRUE EQUALS 6

§ `SAZV § 1(1) and (3)`

-- § 1(1): the Regulation applies to soldiers within the Ministry's remit; § 1(2) takes a posted soldier out of it.
#ASSERT `the Regulation applies to the soldier under the reading` `as printed` (`the soldier who` TRUE "Zentrum Innere Führung" FALSE FALSE 0 0)
#ASSERT NOT (`the Regulation applies to the soldier under the reading` `as printed` (`the soldier who` FALSE "Zentrum Innere Führung" FALSE FALSE 0 0))
#ASSERT NOT (`the Regulation applies to the soldier under the reading` `as printed` (`the soldier who` TRUE "Headquarters Joint Support and Enabling Command" TRUE FALSE 0 0))
#ASSERT `the Regulation applies to the soldier under the reading` `without the establishment the 2025 amending regulation added` (`the soldier who` TRUE "Headquarters Joint Support and Enabling Command" TRUE FALSE 0 0)
-- § 1(3): a soldier with a long-term account posted to an annex establishment keeps § 17, and the account is suspended for the posting.
#ASSERT `the soldier's long-term working-time account is suspended under the reading` `as printed` (`Soldier` WITH `serves within the remit of the Federal Ministry of Defence` IS TRUE, `establishment` IS "Headquarters Joint Support and Enabling Command", `has been transferred or assigned there to perform international or supranational tasks` IS TRUE, `is performing an activity listed in section 30c subsection 4` IS FALSE, `overtime hours ordered or approved this month` IS 0, `hours of time off that compelling service reasons make impossible` IS 0, `has a long-term working-time account` IS TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`the soldier's long-term working-time account is suspended under the reading` `without the establishment the 2025 amending regulation added` (`Soldier` WITH `serves within the remit of the Federal Ministry of Defence` IS TRUE, `establishment` IS "Headquarters Joint Support and Enabling Command", `has been transferred or assigned there to perform international or supranational tasks` IS TRUE, `is performing an activity listed in section 30c subsection 4` IS FALSE, `overtime hours ordered or approved this month` IS 0, `hours of time off that compelling service reasons make impossible` IS 0, `has a long-term working-time account` IS TRUE))
#ASSERT NOT (`the soldier's long-term working-time account is suspended under the reading` `as printed` (`the soldier who` TRUE "Headquarters Joint Support and Enabling Command" TRUE FALSE 0 0))

§ `Grundgesetz Art. 80(1) sentence 3: the 2025 preamble does not cite § 30c(6) with § 93(2) no. 7`

-- The fact this encoding adds to the record: the gazette preamble names eight powers, none of them the exemption power.
#ASSERT NOT (`does the 2025 preamble cite the power to exempt`)
#ASSERT count `the powers cited in the preamble of the 2025 amending regulation` EQUALS 8
-- The original 2015 preamble does not cite it either (sazv-eingangsformel.txt line 2: § 30c Absatz 5 with § 93 Absatz 2 Nummer 5).
#ASSERT NOT (`the preamble cites the power` `the power needed to exempt a group of soldiers` `the powers cited in the original preamble of the SAZV`)
-- Controls: a list that does contain the power tests as cited, and a cited power that is not the one needed does not stand in for it.
#ASSERT `the preamble cites the power` `SG 30c(6) with 93(2) no. 7` (LIST `SG 30c(6) with 93(2) no. 7`, `ArbSiG 38(1)`)
#ASSERT NOT (`the preamble cites the power` `SG 30c(6) with 93(2) no. 7` (LIST `SG 30c(5) sentence 1 no. 2 with 30c(4) and 93(2) no. 6`))
#ASSERT `the 2025 listing is void for want of citation` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`the 2025 listing is void for want of citation` TRUE)
#ASSERT `the reading of the annex to apply` FALSE EQUALS `without the establishment the 2025 amending regulation added`
#ASSERT `the reading of the annex to apply` TRUE EQUALS `as printed`
